    {
      "id": "j1cg1hj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Discovery of the Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Robert Hooke discovered and coined the term 'cell' in 1665 while examining cork tissue.",
        "Matthias Schleiden and Theodor Schwann formulated the Cell Theory, later expanded by Rudolf Virchow.",
        "Cells are classified into Prokaryotes (lacking a membrane-bound nucleus) and Eukaryotes (having a true nucleus).",
        "The cell membrane is a selectively permeable lipid bilayer that regulates the passage of substances into and out of the cell.",
        "Plant cells differ from animal cells by having a rigid cellulose cell wall, chloroplasts, and a large central vacuole."
      ],
      "id": "vsj9004"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lpjv0li",
      "content": "• Robert Hooke discovered the cell in 1665 while observing cork under a microscope."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rn64mzl",
      "content": "• He described the small compartments as 'cells'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7g82cq6",
      "content": "• Anton van Leeuwenhoek later observed living cells using a microscope."
    },
    {
      "id": "5wgkj1w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Cell Theory"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "crsvynb",
      "content": "• All living organisms are composed of cells."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "269li23",
      "content": "• The cell is the basic unit of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "23wnfd1",
      "content": "• All cells arise from pre-existing cells."
    },
    {
