    {
      "id": "hudyc5s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Difference Between Plant Cell and Animal Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Rudolf Virchow added 'Omnis cellula e cellula' (all cells arise from pre-existing cells) to the Cell Theory in 1855.",
        "Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semi-autonomous organelles possessing their own DNA and 70S ribosomes.",
        "Lysosomes are referred to as 'suicidal bags' of the cell because they contain powerful hydrolytic enzymes capable of digesting cellular waste.",
        "Ribosomes are non-membrane-bound organelles responsible for protein synthesis present in both prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells."
      ],
      "id": "38gfm83"
    },
